\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Paired completion-time comparison between modes C and E for 27 matched task blocks across three operators. (a) Each point represents one matched block; points below the identity line have a shorter duration in mode C. (b) Distribution of the paired difference $\Delta T=T_E-T_C$; positive values favor mode C. The violin, horizontal segment, and diamond show the distribution, median, and mean, respectively. The observed mean difference was 1.79 s (matched-block bootstrap 95\% CI, 1.10--2.51 s), and 22/27 blocks favored C; the interval is conditional on the observed blocks.}}{12}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:8}{{8}{12}{}{figure.8}{}}
